-- The converted MP4 moved out of DERIVED_ROOT and in beside its source.
--
-- **There is deliberately no data rewrite here.** The obvious migration — the
-- one `20260803190000_poster_and_banner_artwork` used when artwork moved — is
-- to rewrite the keys and abandon the old files, because a poster is
-- regenerated by the next probe. A transcode is hours of CPU, and for a video
-- whose source has been reclaimed the converted file is the only copy of the
-- film. Rewriting these keys without moving the bytes would point every
-- already-converted row at a file that is not there.
--
-- SQL cannot move a file, so the move is `POST /admin/jobs/relocate-conversions`
-- instead, and rows keep working under either layout until it has run
-- (`playbackRoot` in src/transcode/converted-key.ts decides which root a key is
-- relative to). `JobsService.onModuleInit` logs a warning naming the endpoint
-- while any row is still under the old prefix.
--
-- The index is the part that has to be here. Two rows sharing one converted
-- file is silent corruption rather than an error — both stream it, and deleting
-- either takes the other's only playable copy. Existing values are
-- `converted/<cuid>.mp4` and so unique by construction, and Postgres permits
-- many NULLs, so this builds cleanly and leaves unconverted rows alone.

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX "Video_playbackKey_key" ON "Video"("playbackKey");
